---
// How the site is made, and what it does not do.
import TextPage from '../components/i/TextPage.astro';

const updated = new Date().toLocaleDateString('en-GB', { day: 'numeric', month: 'long', year: 'numeric' });
---

<TextPage
  title="Colophon · Robert Straubmüller"
  description="How straubmueller.com is made: Astro, Remotion films, three typefaces, no cookies."
  heading="Colophon"
>
  <h2>Built</h2>
  <p>
    A static site made with Astro and hosted by webgo in Germany. I designed it and built it with Claude Code as my
    pair programmer. The code is public on <a href="https://github.com/RobStraubm/straubmueller.com">GitHub</a>, so you
    can see how it was made, commit by commit.
  </p>

  <h2>Films</h2>
  <p>
    The short films next to the projects are drawn in code with Remotion, one stage per project that changes over three
    acts. Every word and number in them comes from the project's own material: slides, wireframes, test results and
    commits. Where something is only an illustration, such as text drawn as bars, the film does not pretend it is data.
  </p>

  <h2>Type</h2>
  <p>Schibsted Grotesk for text, Noto Serif Display and Fragment Mono for details. All three are free and served from this site.</p>

  <h2>Privacy</h2>
  <p>No cookies, no tracking, no analytics, nothing loaded from other servers. Details are in the <a href="/datenschutz">Datenschutz</a>.</p>

  <p>Last updated {updated}.</p>
</TextPage>
